{{/* @dot donseba/go-webthings-docs/internal/website.DocsArticleData */}}
<article class="grid max-w-5xl gap-6">
    {{ template "hero.gohtml" . }}

<pre><code>info := form.Info{
    Target: "/contacts", Method: http.MethodPost,
    SubmitText: "Save contact",
    CancelTarget: "/contacts", CancelText: "Cancel",
    Attributes: map[string]string{"class": "contact-form"},
}
model := form.WithRequestInfo(r, input, info)</code></pre>
<p><code>WithRequestInfo</code> returns a <code>RenderModel</code> pairing the input with metadata. It copies the request’s CSRF token into the form info. The token is only there when the renderer’s CSRF middleware handled the request first; without the middleware the form renders without one. A <code>class</code> or <code>style</code> in <code>Attributes</code> joins the theme’s on the form tag; other attributes render as given.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Helper</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>WithInfo(model, info)</code></td><td>Rendering without a request; no automatic token injection</td></tr><tr><td><code>WithContextInfo(ctx, model, info)</code></td><td>Metadata plus a token present on the context</td></tr><tr><td><code>WithRequestInfo(r, model, info)</code></td><td>The usual HTTP rendering helper</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>Template data</h2>
<pre><code>type ContactPage struct {
    Form form.RenderModel
    Errors form.FieldErrors
}</code></pre>
<pre><code>{{"{{"}} form_render .Form .Errors }}</code></pre>
<p>The wrapper is transparent to field transformation, so input fields keep their names and nesting. Embedding <code>form.Info</code> as the first field of the input is also supported, but is optional.</p>
<h2>More form settings</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>Info.ReadOnly</code></td><td>Every field renders disabled and there is no submit button; a cancel link still shows, as a way back.</td></tr><tr><td><code>Info.Hidden</code></td><td>Hidden inputs the form sends along, such as the page to return to (<code>url.Values</code>).</td></tr><tr><td><code>Info.IDPrefix</code></td><td>A prefix for the ids of the form’s fields, for several forms on one page.</td></tr><tr><td><code>Info.Honeypot</code></td><td>The name of a spam trap field; see below.</td></tr><tr><td><code>RenderModel.Overrides</code></td><td>Struct tags replaced for this render, such as a maximum that depends on the places left (<a href="{{ basePath }}/fields" hx-get="{{ basePath }}/fields" hx-target="#content" hx-push-url="true">fields</a>).</td></tr><tr><td><code>RenderModel.Options</code></td><td>The choices of fields only known at render time (<a href="{{ basePath }}/fields" hx-get="{{ basePath }}/fields" hx-target="#content" hx-push-url="true">fields</a>).</td></tr><tr><td><code>RenderModel.Carry</code></td><td>A failed submission shown again after a redirect (<a href="{{ basePath }}/submissions" hx-get="{{ basePath }}/submissions" hx-target="#content" hx-push-url="true">submissions</a>).</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p><code>Hidden</code> and <code>IDPrefix</code> are described with <a href="{{ basePath }}/layout" hx-get="{{ basePath }}/layout" hx-target="#content" hx-push-url="true">laying out fields</a>. Set <code>RenderModel</code> fields on the value <code>WithInfo</code> or <code>WithRequestInfo</code> returns.</p>
<h2>A spam honeypot</h2>
<pre><code>model := form.WithRequestInfo(r, input, form.Info{Target: "/contact", Method: "post", Honeypot: "website"})

if form.IsSpam(r, "website") {
    http.Redirect(w, r, "/contact?sent=1", http.StatusSeeOther)
    return
}</code></pre>
<p>The honeypot is a text field hidden from people and screen readers, which many bots fill in. <code>IsSpam</code> reports whether it was filled in; answer such a request as if it succeeded, without storing or sending anything. The field stays a normal text input, which bots do not skip. Themes hide it with <code>ThemeClasses.Honeypot</code>; the built-in Bootstrap and Tailwind themes use a class and no inline style, so it also stays hidden under a Content-Security-Policy that refuses inline styles. A form whose markup you write yourself renders it with <code>{{"{{"}} form_honeypot "website" }}</code>.</p>
<h2>Explicit token helpers</h2>
<p><code>GetCSRFToken(r)</code> reads the request token. <code>InjectCSRFToken</code> and <code>InjectCSRFTokenContext</code> fill an existing info value. Usually the <code>WithRequestInfo</code> wrapper avoids that manual step.</p>
<p>Attribute names and form targets should come from trusted application configuration. Keep per-request metadata local rather than mutating a shared info value.</p>
</article>
